      <div class="hcm-or-hd"><span class="hcm-or-eyebrow">Feature Checklist</span><h2>Kyota Feature Checklist: What to Verify Before You Buy</h2></div>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px">Before choosing a Kyota model, compare both <strong style="color:var(--ink)">hardware and software</strong>. Hardware includes the <strong style="color:var(--ink)">massage rollers</strong>, foot and calf system, <strong style="color:var(--ink)">heating modules located</strong> in the chair, recline design, and frame fit. Software includes auto programs, scanning, intensity adjustments, <strong style="color:var(--ink)">intelligent voice command control</strong> if available, and any <strong style="color:var(--ink)">customized massage specific</strong> settings.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px">Do not assume every Kyota model includes the same features. If <strong style="color:var(--ink)">gravity reclining, weightless zero gravity recline, wall fit space saving, fit space saving technology, shiatsu rollers per foot, complete calf kneading oscillation</strong>, or a <strong style="color:var(--ink)">quick access control panel</strong> matter to you, verify those features on the individual product page or with an HCM specialist.</p>
      <p>Body fit also matters. <strong style="color:var(--ink)">User size and shape</strong> can affect how well the chair maps the shoulders, back, calves, and feet. Some advanced systems may help <strong style="color:var(--ink)">pinpoint the user size</strong> or use body <strong style="color:var(--ink)">shape, providing a customized</strong> experience, but you should not rely only on the <strong style="color:var(--ink)">chair to pinpoint</strong> your fit. Try the chair in person when possible. The right chair should <strong style="color:var(--ink)">provide a soothing</strong> daily routine without feeling too aggressive or too light. State of the art features only matter if they improve your daily use. Zero gravity can create a <strong style="color:var(--ink)">sense of weightlessness</strong> for many users. Avoid <strong style="color:var(--ink)">sliding the chair</strong> across flooring after setup; confirm placement before delivery.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

